<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bryn Derwin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1255</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bryn Derwin was fought in June 1255 at a pass in the hills of Caernarfonshire, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> defeated his brothers Owain and Dafydd, with whom he had shared Gwynedd. Llywelyn imprisoned Owain and became sole ruler of Gwynedd west of the Conwy, the base from which he made himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bryn-derwin.jpg" alt="Battle of Bryn Derwin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eric Jones · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boggy_land_in_the_col_between_Y_Foel_and_Mynydd_Cennin_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1798532.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
